# TLS certificates and keys -- GENERATED, never committed.
#
# They used to be tracked, which had two costs. The README tells operators to
# regenerate for their own IP (`rm -rf certs/ && bash scripts/gen-certs.sh`), and
# following that instruction left nine modified tracked files and one deletion in
# the working tree forever -- so `git status` stopped being useful and real
# changes hid in the noise. Worse, the obvious way out of that state,
# `git add -A`, commits the operator's own PRIVATE KEYS over the shipped ones.
#
# scripts/setup.sh generates them on first run, the same way it does
# run/secrets.env, so a fresh clone still works with no extra step -- and every
# install now has its own CA instead of one whose private key is public.
certs/

# Runtime data
run/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Documentation with sensitive data
SERVER_RUNNING.md

